nings** indicate potential conflicts but the binding may still work.\"].join(`\n/bin/claude:8394:`}return _.trim()}function mK5(){return}var IK5;var pK5=L(()=>{KT();IK5=[\"the\",\"a\",\"an\",\"I\",\"you\",\"he\",\"she\",\"it\",\"we\",\"they\",\"me\",\"him\",\"her\",\"us\",\"them\",\"my\",\"your\",\"his\",\"its\",\"our\",\"this\",\"that\",\"what\",\"who\",\"is\",\"are\",\"was\",\"were\",\"be\",\"been\",\"have\",\"has\",\"had\",\"do\",\"does\",\"did\",\"will\",\"would\",\"can\",\"could\",\"may\",\"might\",\"must\",\"shall\",\"should\",\"make\",\"made\",\"get\",\"got\",\"go\",\"went\",\"come\",\"came\",\"see\",\"saw\",\"know\",\"take\",\"think\",\"look\",\"want\",\"use\",\"find\",\"give\",\"tell\",\"work\",\"call\",\"try\",\"ask\",\"need\",\"feel\",\"seem\",\"leave\",\"put\",\"time\",\"year\",\"day\",\"way\",\"man\",\"thing\",\"life\",\"hand\",\"part\",\"place\",\"case\",\"point\",\"fact\",\"good\",\"new\",\"first\",\"last\",\"long\",\"great\",\"little\",\"own\",\"other\",\"old\",\"right\",\"big\",\"high\",\"small\",\"large\",\"next\",\"early\",\"young\",\"few\",\"public\",\"bad\",\"same\",\"able\",\"in\",\"on\",\"at\",\"to\",\"for\",\"of\",\"with\",\"from\",\"by\",\"about\",\"like\",\"through\",\"over\",\"before\",\"between\",\"under\",\"since\",\"without\",\"and\",\"or\",\"but\",\"if\",\"than\",\"because\",\"as\",\"until\",\"while\",\"so\",\"though\",\"both\",\"each\",\"when\",\"where\",\"why\",\"how\",\"not\",\"now\",\"just\",\"more\",\"also\",\"here\",\"there\",\"then\",\"only\",\"very\",\"well\",\"back\",\"still\",\"even\",\"much\",\"too\",\"such\",\"never\",\"again\",\"most\",\"once\",\"off\",\"away\",\"down\",\"out\",\"up\",\"test\",\"code\",\"data\",\"file\",\"line\",\"text\",\"word\",\"number\",\"system\",\"program\",\"set\",\"run\",\"value\",\"name\",\"type\",\"state\",\"end\",\"start\"]});function BK5(){return}var gK5=L(()=>{Tw();KT()});function FK5(){Ow({name:\"simplify\",description:\"Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\",userInvocable:!0,async getPromptForCommand(q){let K=d8O;if(q)K+=`\n/bin/claude:8398:${q}`;return[{type:\"text\",text:K}]}})}var d8O;var UK5=L(()=>{pY();KT();d8O=`# Simplify: Code Review and Cleanup\n/bin/claude:8400:Review all changed files for reuse, quality, and efficiency. Fix any issues found.\n/bin/claude:8404:Run \\`git diff\\` (or \\`git diff HEAD\\` if there are staged changes) to see what changed. If there are no git changes, review the most recently modified files that the user mentioned or that you edited earlier in this conversation.\n/bin/claude:8406:## Phase 2: Launch Three Review Agents in Parallel\n/bin/claude:8410:### Agent 1: Code Reuse Review\n/bin/claude:8418:### Agent 2: Code Quality Review\n/bin/claude:8420:Review the same changes for hacky patterns:\n/bin/claude:8430:### Agent 3: Efficiency Review\n/bin/claude:8432:Review the same changes for efficiency:\n/bin/claude:8437:4. **Recurring no-op updates**: state/store updates inside polling loops, intervals, or event handlers that fire unconditionally — add a change-detection guard so downstream consumers aren't notified when nothing changed. Also: if a wrapper function takes an updater/reducer callback, verify it honors same-reference returns (or whatever the \"no change\" signal is) — otherwise callers' early-return no-ops are silently defeated\n/bin/claude:8439:6. **Memory**: unbounded data structures, missing cleanup, event listener leaks\n/bin/claude:8478:### Step 2: Interview the User\n/bin/claude:8503:- How should the skill be executed? (e.g. always use a Task agent to conduct code review, or invoke an agent team for a set of concurrent steps)\n/bin/claude:8514:Stop interviewing once you have enough information. IMPORTANT: Don't over-ask for simple processes!\n/bin/claude:8560:- **Human checkpoint**: When to pause and ask the user before proceeding. Include for irreversible actions (merging, sending messages), error judgment (merge conflicts), or output review.\n/bin/claude:8576:Before writing the file, output the complete SKILL.md content as a yaml code block in your response so the user can review it with proper syntax highlighting. Then ask for confirmation using AskUserQuestion with a simple question like \"Does this SKILL.md look good to save?\" — do NOT use the body field, keep the question concise.\n/bin/claude:8740:Only available for tool events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PermissionRequest.\n/bin/claude:8746:Only available for tool events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PermissionRequest.\n/bin/claude:8846:Given an event, matcher, target file, and desired behavior, follow this flow. Each step catches a different failure class — a hook that silently does nothing is worse than no hook.\n/bin/claude:8848:1. **Dedup check.** Read the target file. If a hook already exists on the same event+matcher, show the existing command and ask: keep it, replace it, or add alongside.\n/bin/claude:8867:   \\`jq -e '.hooks.<event>[] | select(.matcher == \"<matcher>\") | .hooks[] | select(.type == \"command\") | .command' <target-file>\\`\n/bin/claude:8879:7. **Handoff.** Tell the user the hook is live (or needs \\`/hooks\\`/restart per the watcher caveat). Point them at \\`/hooks\\` to review, edit, or disable it later. The UI only shows \"Ran N hooks\" if a hook errors or is slow — silent success is invisible by design.\n/bin/claude:8894:**Hook events:** PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PreCompact, PostCompact, Stop, Notification, SessionStart\n/bin/claude:9211:the app. Checking that assertions match source is code review.\n/bin/claude:9251:bare PASS. You're the only reviewer who actually *ran* the thing —\n/bin/claude:9296:**Screenshot / sample:** <the one frame a reviewer looks at to see\n/bin/claude:9308:Lead with ⚠️ for lines worth interrupting the reviewer for — those get\n/bin/claude:9441:      \"events\": [\n/bin/claude:9455:Generate a fresh lowercase UUID for \\`events[].data.uuid\\` yourself.\n/bin/claude:9519:3. **Set the schedule** — Ask when and how often. The user's timezone is ${K}. When they say a time (e.g., \"every morning at 9am\"), assume they mean their local time and convert to UTC for the cron expression. Always confirm the conversion: \"9am ${K} = Xam UTC.\"\n/bin/claude:9522:6. **Review and confirm** — Show the full configuration before creating. Let them adjust.\n/bin/claude:9678:\\`Tool\\` (NOT \\`ToolParam\\`) with an \\`InputSchema\\` record. \\`InputSchema.Type\\` is auto-set to \\`\"object\"\\` by the constructor — don't set it. \\`ToolUnion\\` has an implicit conversion from \\`Tool\\`, triggered by the collection expression \\`[...]\\`.\n/bin/claude:9705:Derived from \\`anthropic-sdk-csharp/src/Anthropic/Models/Messages/Tool.cs\\` and \\`ToolUnion.cs:799\\` (implicit conversion).\n/bin/claude:9717:// No .ToParam() — reconstruct per variant. Implicit conversions from each\n/bin/claude:9847:Effort is nested under \\`OutputConfig\\`, NOT a top-level property. \\`ApiEnum<string, Effort>\\` has an implicit conversion from the enum, so assign \\`Effort.High\\` directly.\n/bin/claude:9859:\\`System\\` takes \\`MessageCreateParamsSystem?\\` — a union of \\`string\\` or \\`List<TextBlockParam>\\`. There is no \\`SystemTextBlockParam\\`; use plain \\`TextBlockParam\\`. The implicit conversion needs the concrete \\`List<TextBlockParam>\\` type (array literals won't convert). For placement patterns and the silent-invalidator audit checklist, see \\`shared/prompt-caching.md\\`.\n/bin/claude:10037:event: message_start\n/bin/claude:10040:event: content_block_start\n/bin/claude:10043:event: content_block_delta\n/bin/claude:10046:event: content_block_stop\n/bin/claude:10049:event: message_delta\n/bin/claude:10052:event: message_stop\n/bin/claude:10240:    event := stream.Current()\n/bin/claude:10241:    switch eventVariant := event.AsAny().(type) {\n/bin/claude:10243:        switch deltaVariant := eventVariant.Delta.AsAny().(type) {\n/bin/claude:10671:        .flatMap(event -> event.contentBlockDelta().stream())\n/bin/claude:11134:foreach ($stream as $event) {\n/bin/claude:11135:    if ($event instanceof RawContentBlockDeltaEvent && $event->delta instanceof TextDelta) {\n/bin/claude:11136:        echo $event->delta->text;\n/bin/claude:11509:        prompt=\"Use the code-reviewer agent to review this codebase\",\n/bin/claude:11513:                \"code-reviewer\": AgentDefinition(\n/bin/claude:11514:                    description=\"Expert code reviewer for quality and security reviews.\",\n/bin/claude:11747:        prompt=\"Review this code\",\n/bin/claude:11750:            system_prompt=\"\"\"You are a senior code reviewer focused on:\n/bin/claude:11928:Hook callback inputs for tool-lifecycle events (\\`PreToolUse\\`, \\`PostToolUse\\`, \\`PostToolUseFailure\\`) include \\`agent_id\\` and \\`agent_type\\` fields, allowing hooks to identify which agent (main or subagent) triggered the tool call.\n/bin/claude:11930:Available hook events: \\`PreToolUse\\`, \\`PostToolUse\\`, \\`PostToolUseFailure\\`, \\`UserPromptSubmit\\`, \\`Stop\\`, \\`SubagentStop\\`, \\`PreCompact\\`, \\`Notification\\`, \\`SubagentStart\\`, \\`PermissionRequest\\`\n/bin/claude:11990:Typed task message subclasses are available for better type safety when handling subagent task events:\n/bin/claude:11992:- \\`TaskProgressMessage\\` — real-time progress updates with cumulative usage metrics\n/bin/claude:12015:    prompt=\"Use the code-reviewer agent to review this codebase\",\n/bin/claude:12019:            \"code-reviewer\": AgentDefinition(\n/bin/claude:12020:                description=\"Expert code reviewer for quality and security reviews.\",\n/bin/claude:12117:5. **Limit max_turns** — Prevent runaway agents with reasonable limits\n/bin/claude:12929:    for event in stream:\n/bin/claude:12930:        if event.type == \"content_block_start\":\n/bin/claude:12931:            if event.content_block.type == \"thinking\":\n/bin/claude:12933:            elif event.content_block.type == \"text\":\n/bin/claude:12936:        elif event.type == \"content_block_delta\":\n/bin/claude:12937:            if event.delta.type == \"thinking_delta\":\n/bin/claude:12938:                print(event.delta.thinking, end=\"\", flush=True)\n/bin/claude:12939:            elif event.delta.type == \"text_delta\":\n/bin/claude:12940:                print(event.delta.text, end=\"\", flush=True)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
